:You didn't really deserve to get flamed.  They probably just didn't
:believe you.  If I eat when not satiated I can't recall ever choking.
:The code in pl7 at least checks for this explicitly.  Perhaps you
:encountered a bug.  Which patchlevel?
     Most likely the most recent, based on what I remember of his
previous posts.  
     I don't have access to the code.  If anyone does, check in there
for the food item that has the most "nutrition per turn" content.  Then
check the number of food turns between "satiated" and "choked."  Or,
alternatively, go into wizard mode, get satiated, wait until one is not
satiated by one turn, and try eating such a food item.  If one can choke
that way, we have a problem.  If not, the guy is either lying, hit a
game bug, or hit some very insidious line noise.  Simple enough, IMO.
